WEBVTT

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.670
Before we tour our next property,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.920
I'd like for us to make
a brief stop. Is that all right?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.630
Of course. Where are we gonna stop?

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.930
The Crone's Lair.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.600
<i>More </i>scary places?!

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.640
I need to return the bed
they provided for you.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.600
Return it?

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.730
Wait, don't tell me
we have to go back to get it!

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.310
No, I've brought it with me.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.270
Wait, how? It's huge!

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.110
It's in here.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:17.120
It's an adventuring staple: a bag that
can hold any item, regardless of size.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.280
Isn't that just a Bag of Hol--

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.950
It's a satchel.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:25.120
"My First Home"

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.670
They run their showroom out of this cave?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.180
Yes, that's right.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.470
These ladies have been in business
here for just about a thousand years.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.770
Welcome.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.600
It's been too long, Dear Boy.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.810
Finally ready to make us
good, honest women, eh?

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.610
These are the Graiae Sisters,
skillful craftswomen and frequent buyers.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.900
You our Dear Boy's latest charge?

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.910
Yes. My name's Letty.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.580
We usually turn away newcomers like you.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.910
But we'll make an
exception for our Dear Boy.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.620
Take a good ol' look at our goodies
here and learn a thing or two.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.670
We got everything you could ever need.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.510
Whether you're a tiny pixie...

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.680
Or a towerin' giant.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.300
Look at the size of this door!

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.890
They have dragon-sized doors as well.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.980
Huh? Where's the doorknob?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.940
The knobs are sold separately,
and for a reason.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.320
By inserting a different magic knob,
you can travel to different locations.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.900
Wow, that's pretty neat!

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.360
Lemme give it a try.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.160
--How goes business?
--It's been rough for everyone.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.990
If only we coulda made off
with that dragon...

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.000
Should we put together
a squad to capture it again?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.620
Not a bad idea.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.630
Nope, nothing to see there.
Nothing to hear there, either.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.340
Is everything all right?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.170
A youngin' like you might
like somethin' more like this.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.720
Don't go oglin' it too hard though, aight?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.970
Behold, the Gate of the Gallant Lady!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.630
BA-BUMP!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.640
The painting's alive!

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.140
That's incredible!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.480
Simply tell her the magic word
and the door will open for you.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.600
It will?

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.110
You must do so
within the time limit, however.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.610
I'm afraid you are out of time.
Now, for a reading.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.320
Fail to do so, and she shall read one
of your embarrassing poems out loud.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.570
Why?!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.820
"My Flame of Love," by Letty.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.990
"Our meeting was a
fateful spark of destiny.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:29.710
Now, my flame of love for
you burns hotter every day.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.840
Though it burns and
scalds my hollow body,

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.380
my happiness knows no end,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.300
because this burning pain is
proof of my burning love for you."

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.220
Please, stop!

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.930
How am I supposed
to come back from that...

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.690
Don't be a baby.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.690
A single beam of light, shining from
the heavens to balm my wounded soul!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.450
Don't go into the light, Letty.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.700
It's just a fixture, after all.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.160
Yeah, figured.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.240
Whoa, what's that?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.040
Th-There's something in there!

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.120
Yes, a salamander.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.500
But why?!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.590
They're serving a jail sentence for arson.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:20.470
While they're servin' time, they work
as magic lanterns, givin' off light.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:24.720
You don't need to give 'em any fuel.
Just watch your fingers around 'em.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.680
If they get too ornery, just
dump 'em in a bucket of water.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.600
That'll set 'em straight.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.560
Elderly wisdom at its finest.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.650
We got some'a these;
we got some'a those...

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:38.320
Letty, I see some furniture over there.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.030
Wow! What a cute little fireplace!

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:47.790
If I had one of these,
I could do this, or maybe even this...

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.870
Woulda thought he'd dream bigger.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.250
What kinda dragon is this?

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.750
Shoulda been born a newt.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.330
That dog's a bit too big,
wouldn't you agree?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.630
That fireplace's built from brick
forged in the primeval flame.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.430
It can withstand your fire breath, too,
so it's real good for dragon folk.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.140
There is one drawback, however.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.640
It weighs a hundred tons!

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.720
Oh, jeez!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.350
The average structure's floor would
surely collapse under the weight of it.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.640
Yeah...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.730
However, if you built a house
from the ground up,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.270
you could plan for that weight
and adjust the schematics accordingly.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.940
Build a house?

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.200
Well, that ain't happenin'.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.070
Why're you worryin' about the floor
when you should be worryin' about <i>cash</i>?

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.290
You even got the money
to build a whole house?

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.700
Oh, uh...

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.250
We'll buy your wings off ya if you want.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.580
Would you like to build one?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.170
I have a prime location in mind for you,

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.880
and we can always discuss
cost after our consultation.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.300
Would you be up for it, then?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.890
But what would we build?

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.390
Your very own house, Letty.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.680
What?!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.270
Land for Sale

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.270
Elf Housing Realty

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:12.790
Yoo-hoo! Yoo-hoo!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.790
They're here.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:15.330
What an incredible view!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.080
Yes, it's what makes
this location so wonderful.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.590
Hold on, though, Dearia.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:23.550
I'm really excited to build a house,

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.550
but I don't know if I have enough money.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.970
Not to worry.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.470
When you consider the cumulative
worth of your organs and material drops,

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.060
you can afford whatever you like.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.100
I won't be <i>alive </i>to live there!

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.310
Fear not, I'm only kidding.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.350
How much money do you have on hand,
if you don't mind my asking?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.520
Hold on a sec, lemme get my wallet.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.240
Ah, yes, dragons do prefer to keep
valuables behind their inverted scales.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:49.240
Yeah, it's great for
holding little things!

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.490
That's why dragons get so mad
when people try to touch them there.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.490
Get your paws off me!

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.500
Plus, it's not like we
could carry a bag around.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.000
True.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.000
My...

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:02.920
Is this a tooth?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.260
Yeah, it's one of my baby teeth.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:12.850
I heard a fairy will turn them into
money if I put them under my pillow,

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.850
so I held onto them just in case!

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.850
Here you go!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.270
I hate to tell you this,
but that is merely a fanciful story.

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:18.510
Noooo!

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:21.440
Holding onto them
won't turn them into money.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.900
Guess that means I'm broke.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.650
Not to worry. Dragon teeth do sell well.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.570
Really?

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:31.280
Though adult teeth are
worth more than baby teeth.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.990
You needn't worry.
The money problem will solve itself.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.950
What do you mean?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.210
You'll find out soon enough.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:43.540
By now, I have a fair grasp
on your tastes and desires.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.090
I've taken the liberty of designing
the interior and exterior for you.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:50.550
Here we have the living space.
The fireplace goes here.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.220
The kitchen is in this section here.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.600
I love it!

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.520
Excellent. Let us get right
to constructing it, then.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.400
Come, friends, gather 'round.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.530
Wh-What's happening?!

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:14.580
These are my employees.
Here, we have gnomes.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.830
They're quite skilled at construction.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:19.870
Here, we have our ogres.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.750
They will assist with the heavy lifting.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.790
Oh, but first...

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.510
Would you like a traditional
Shinto groundbreaking ceremony?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.840
No, thank you, I'm not Shinto.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.470
Then how about a nice human sacrifice?

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.680
No, thank you!

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.850
Do be careful to avoid injury on the job.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.440
I hope this'll all work out...

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.320
Wow!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.910
S-Sorry!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.910
I gotta be careful.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.830
Excellent work.
Please place that over there.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.540
Hey, Dearia.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.840
Is there anything I can help with?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.380
I probably can't do any heavy lifting,

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.800
or anything that needs a special skill...

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.720
Now that I think of it,
I might not be able to help out at all.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.930
Come, now. Enough self-deprecating talk.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.520
You can assist with the fireproofing
of the lumber, if you'd like.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.140
On it! I can handle that!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.070
I think I pissed them off!

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:40.910
Use less? Keep it more even? No?

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.170
My, Letty.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.460
Whomever did you
battle to end up like that?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.220
I-I was completely outmatched.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.430
Did you lose?

00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:01.180
I got destroyed. They said my work
was "garbage" and shooed me away.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.350
What are <i>you </i>doing, Dearia?

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.390
I'm making quicklime mortar.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.480
Whoa, what's that do?

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.940
It's essentially a very moist plaster.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.070
Cool!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:14.360
It's top-of-the-line, aged for ten years.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:21.950
Would you like to help?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.040
I'd love to!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.410
Do I just need to mix it?

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:28.670
Yes. We'll be adding aggregate to it
to make mortar for the outer walls.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:33.510
Instead of gravel,
we will use golem scurf.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.880
Golem what?!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.970
It will make the walls extremely sturdy.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.770
Sorry.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.610
T'would seem we've created
a new breed of dragon.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:52.360
Here.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.570
Th-Thank you.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.780
Letty.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.240
No need to rush.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.490
We'll get this done, <i>together</i>.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.500
Right!

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.480
It's done!

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:34.650
Thank you so much, everyone!
You did a great job.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.900
I can't thank you enough!

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.610
I finally own my dream home!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.870
Now we wait for the Heroes to come.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.700
What? Why?!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:51.830
How will we pay off the building costs
without selling fallen Hero equipment?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.550
<i>That's </i>what you meant
by the problem "solving itself"?!

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.050
No way!

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.510
There's no need to worry, Letty.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:03.220
I can't have Heroes coming here!

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:03.220
I've called forth
a few brilliant fighters.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.520
Th-They look scary!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.230
You're...

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.940
I'm...?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.990
You're so cool!

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.860
I am?

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:22.990
A real-life dragon!

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:23.820
I can't believe it!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.700
Holy crap, dude!

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.040
These will be your
live-in security guards.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:31.540
They may seem a little off at
first-glance, but they're fine people.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.380
You're right! They're really nice!

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.500
Fifty percent of the spoils from Hero
attacks will go to their salary,

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.300
while the other fifty percent will
go towards the land and construction.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.930
Don't worry, boss, you can
count on us to keep you safe!

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:43.300
Sounds great!

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:44.720
Let's do this, dudes!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.810
Yeah!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:50.560
Right, then, I'll come by every
few days to check up on you.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.400
Thank you so much for the trouble.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:58.030
Do enjoy your new
living arrangements, Letty.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.710
I never <i>dreamed </i>I'd be living a cushy life
in a wonderful house like this...

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.630
Excellent.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.510
So <i>this </i>is our newest dungeon!

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:27.930
With me, friends!

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.720
For loot and glory!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.450
These hallways sure are huge.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.040
Let's be extra careful.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.580
Worry not, mage.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.500
It's not like we'll get
TPK'd out of nowhere!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.300
Except that literally just happened to us.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:03.130
Stay close, comrades!

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.770
Huh? What's that noise?!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:17.810
Beware: guards

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:22.320
What are you guys doing?!

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:24.070
Oh! Hey, Letty!

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:26.410
Don't worry, we got it handled!

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:28.200
But the wall...

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:33.160
We will not accept defeat at
the hands of an agent of darkness!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:38.000
Well you better, 'cause you ain't
beating us! Wanna know why?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.210
Our boss is a <i>dragon</i>!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:44.210
Don't drag me into this!

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.050
You! I remember you!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.430
The deadly dragon!

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:50.550
It wasn't me; I swear!

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.220
We'll let you off with
just your gear this time!

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.480
Now get outta here
before we burn you to a crisp!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:02.600
Equipment Lost

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.690
Mark my words,
we <i>will </i>return to defeat you,

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.400
Flame Dragon Lord of Mass Destruction!

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.410
The Heroes gave him a long, cringey name.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:11.450
--Retreat, friends!
--We'll be back!

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.200
Nice going!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.620
Those Heroes ain't no match for us!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.710
Dragons are so fierce!

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.790
We're invincible!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.340
My heart can't take this...

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.180
I'm not that kind of dragon!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:34.520
Hey, boss! You got a visitor!

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.060
I wonder who'd wanna visit me.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.070
Wait, where are they?

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.900
There on the chair, boss.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:46.860
On the chair?

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.610
Lord... Lord...

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.200
Flame Dragon Lord!

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.910
There they are!

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.700
Flame Dragon Lord,
we beseech you!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:02.420
Let us shelter in the refuge
of your almighty strength!

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:06.590
Our kind is weak and frail,
and we fear for our very lives!

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:10.050
I mean, thanks, but I'm not really...

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:15.470
We've heard Heroes tell of
your terrifying, fearsome power!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.940
That's how they're putting it?!

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:22.900
I mean, it's just two of you, right?

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.690
And I've got lots of rooms.
Feel free to stay.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.570
We're forever in your debt, milord!

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.530
Yo, boss.

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:32.160
It's not just those two.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.570
What?

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.910
Flame Dragon Lord!

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:38.500
We heard you defeated those
Heroes with a single fatal blow!

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.160
Please, help us!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.460
We heard you burned down
everything in a one-mile radius!

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:44.630
Your Excellency!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.800
We heard you destroyed
an entire kingdom in a single night!

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.170
You got a bunch of new underlings, too!

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:55.510
The Heroes are here! Get 'em, guys!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.440
Whaddya want us to do with 'em?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:06.610
Wanna kill 'em?

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:08.440
Please just let them go.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.900
We caught ourselves a thief!

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.360
You don't have to come show me!

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.740
Your Excellency, to honor your kindness
and show our appreciation,

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:18.870
we have composed an ode
telling of your great deeds!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.830
♬ Oh, the Great Flame Dragon Lord! ♬

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.920
Please, stop!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.130
♬ Great, glorious, and good! ♬

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.130
Your Excellency!

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:36.220
♬ All hail our beloved
Flame Dragon Lord! ♬

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:32.420
Our house made the rankings for Top Ten
Dungeons Great Heroes <i>have </i>to Raid!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.220
Congratulations, boss!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:39.220
Three cheers for the Flame Dragon Lord!

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:46.480
Hip hip hooray! Hip hip hooray!
Hip hip hooray! Hip hip hooray!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.280
"Please don't come looking for me.
--Letty"

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.200
Oh, dear.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.040
Letty?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.550
O-Oh, Dearia!

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:18.300
I stopped by to visit, but you weren't
at home. Is everything all right?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.230
I see. That must be overwhelming.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:27.440
Yeah. I know everyone means well.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:33.490
And I <i>do </i>wanna help everyone
who doesn't have a home, too.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:37.910
But every time they call me
the Flame Dragon Lord,

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:42.040
I feel so much pressure on me...

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.540
That, and...

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:48.630
I really don't want my home
to be everyone's favorite dungeon!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:58.340
I just want somewhere
I can live in peace and quiet.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.720
Very well.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.890
Let us find you a house
with that purpose in mind.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.310
Really? B-But...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:11.110
I don't want to trouble you
with all this again!

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.780
It's all right.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:17.400
My other dragon friend also
eventually found a home of his own.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.780
It only took a hundred years.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:22.120
And that's "all right" to you?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:27.920
A hundred years is the twinkling
of an eye to my long-lived kind.

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.670
Yes, we encountered
our share of trouble along the way...

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:38.260
...but those years we spent
together were truly meaningful.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:44.060
It is not your place to decide
what troubles me, Letty.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.060
Not once has your plight
troubled me in the slightest.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:52.020
So allow me to help you find a home.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:21:04.450
I know we will find
your perfect home someday.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.330
I feel bad for leaving
without saying anything.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.790
Not to worry.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:11.750
Huh?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.290
Let's put your belongings
into my satchel, yes?

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:17.340
I've already handled the situation.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:20.970
I know I can trust you to hold the fort.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:23.850
Please keep everyone safe.
Till we meet again!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.220
Boss!

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:29.600
They gladly bought the property from you.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.560
You're making me sound <i>way </i>too cool!

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:35.190
Hold on a sec, Dearia.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:38.940
Did you know this was gonna happen?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.160
What? No. Of course not. I would never.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:49.290
Why the heck didn't you <i>tell </i>me then?!

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:52.250
I anticipated there may be
a few issues along the way.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:55.540
I certainly didn't predict
trouble of this magnitude.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:58.300
So you <i>did </i>think there'd be trouble!

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:02.630
The weak little dragon's
journey seems set to continue.

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:34.050
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:34.100
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:34.140
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.890
Are you thinking of
building your own home?

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:37.940
Then I'm sure you're
wondering about taxes.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.020
Taxes on Newly Built Structures

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:40.270
Structures are subject
to a consumption tax,

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:42.150
Building Fees + Tax

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:41.980
but land is not.

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.060
Only pay 
price for land!

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:44.860
This is because structures
deteriorate, but land does not.

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:47.240
Next time, "A Cold Home."

